# Node
node_modules/

# Scratch output from the check scripts and exported tuning files
*.tmp.json
*.bak
*.bak.*

# Local tooling / secrets
# .claude/* rather than .claude/ so the skills dir can be re-included below:
# git cannot re-include a path whose parent directory is itself excluded.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
# ⛔ settings.json is TRACKED on purpose. It installs the boundary guard (tools/guard_boundary.php):
# the gates on pushing, on moving `main`, and on the spec. Left ignored, the guardrail would exist on one
# machine, unrecorded, and a fresh clone would silently have no boundary at all. settings.local.json stays
# ignored: that one is machine-local convenience, not enforcement.
!.claude/settings.json
# .claude/rules/ is TRACKED: Claude-Code-only notes that load alongside AGENTS.md (the shared brief).
!.claude/rules/
# .vibe/* rather than .vibe/ so the two files below can be re-included (same reason as .claude/*).
.vibe/*
# ⛔ hooks.toml and config.toml are TRACKED on purpose. hooks.toml installs the boundary for Mistral Vibe
# (tools/guard_boundary_vibe.php, an adapter over tools/guard_boundary.php). A guard that is not tracked
# does not exist on a fresh clone — Vibe would run with no boundary and nothing would say so. Anything
# else under .vibe/ is machine-local and stays ignored.
!.vibe/hooks.toml
!.vibe/config.toml
.env
*.local

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
